Plumb messages: a swept selection, a bare click that expands to a word, and a
click between blank lines that expands to nothing (no message). The host builds
each plumb message (Hplumb) and writes the packed bytes to the terminal. The
payload's wdir is an absolute path, so the transcript shows only the message
name while the raw-byte comparison checks the full content against C.

-- input --
alpha

beta
gamma
-- proto --
Hversion 2
Hnewname tag=0
Hmovname tag=0 "input"
Tversion 2
Tstartcmdfile
Hnewname tag=1
Hbindname tag=1
Hcurrent tag=1
Hmovname tag=1 "~~sam~~"
Hcheck0 tag=1
Hack
Tack
Hunlock
Tstartfile 0
Hbindname tag=0
Hcurrent tag=0
Hgrow tag=0 p=0 n=18
Hcheck0 tag=0
Hcheck0 tag=0
Hack
Trequest 0 0 18
Hdata tag=0 p=0 "alpha\n\nbeta\ngamma\n"
Tack
Hgrow tag=1 p=0 n=10
Hcheck0 tag=1
Hack
Trequest 1 0 10
Hdata tag=1 p=0 " +. input\n"
Tack
Hsetdot tag=1 p=10 n=10
Hunlock
Tplumb 0 0 5
Hplumb
Tplumb 0 8 8
Hplumb
Tplumb 0 6 6
Texit
